---
import Base from "../../layouts/Base.astro";
import { CONTACT_EMAIL, POLICY_UPDATED } from "../../components/site-data";
---
<Base
  title="Terms · Is There a Burn Ban?"
  description="Is There a Burn Ban? summarizes official burn ban sources for information only. Always confirm with the official source before you burn."
  path="/terms/"
>
  <main id="content" class="page">
    <nav class="crumbs" aria-label="Breadcrumb">
      <ol>
        <li><a href="/">Home</a></li>
        <li aria-current="page">Terms</li>
      </ol>
    </nav>
    <h1>Terms</h1>
    <p class="muted">Updated {POLICY_UPDATED}.</p>

    <h2 id="informational">Informational only</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>
        Burn bans are set by state, county, city, tribal and federal officials. We are not one of them. We read their public
        feeds and pages and summarize what they say.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Always confirm with the official source before you burn.</strong> Every status links to it. Cities, fire
        districts and land managers can have stricter rules than the county.
      </li>
      <li>"Not sure" (<code>unknown</code>) never means burning is allowed. It means we can't confirm the status.</li>
      <li>
        Sources can be late, wrong or offline, and we can make mistakes copying them. Alerts can be delayed or not arrive.
        Don't rely on this site or its alerts as your only check.
      </li>
    </ul>

    <h2 id="warranty">No warranty</h2>
    <p>
      The site, API, MCP server and alerts are free and provided "as is", without warranties of any kind. To the extent the
      law allows, we aren't liable for losses from using them, including fines, fire damage or missed alerts.
    </p>

    <h2 id="data">Using the data</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>
        Statuses are facts summarized from public agencies. When you show one, name the source and link the official page
        we give you (<code>officialUrl</code>).
      </li>
      <li>
        Some publishers limit reuse. For example, Texas A&amp;M Forest Service data is for noncommercial use with
        attribution. Check each source's terms before you republish in bulk. See <a href="/data/">the dataset page</a>.
      </li>
      <li>
        The API and MCP server need no key. Please cache responses for a few minutes and keep request rates reasonable. We
        may limit or block traffic that degrades the service, and endpoints can change.
      </li>
    </ul>

    <h2 id="alerts">Alerts</h2>
    <p>
      Email alerts are double opt-in and every email has an unsubscribe link. You can turn push alerts off at any time. See
      <a href="/privacy/">privacy</a> for what we store.
    </p>

    <h2 id="changes">Changes and contact</h2>
    <p>
      We may update these terms; the date above shows the last change. Questions: <a href={`mailto:${CONTACT_EMAIL}`}>{CONTACT_EMAIL}</a>.
    </p>
  </main>
</Base>
